---
import BaseLayout from "../components/BaseLayout.astro";
import { absoluteUrl, href } from "../lib/paths";

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "AboutPage",
  name: "About Move-Out Desk",
  url: absoluteUrl("/about"),
  description:
    "Independence and affiliate disclosure for Move-Out Desk, a Texas A&M storage comparison.",
  isPartOf: { "@type": "WebSite", name: "Move-Out Desk", url: absoluteUrl("/") },
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About this comparison and the affiliate disclosure"
  description="Move-Out Desk is independent of Texas A&M and of the storage companies it lists. No affiliate programs are joined. If a link is ever paid, it will be marked."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <p class="crumbs"><a href={href("/")}>Home</a> / About</p>
  <p class="eyebrow">Disclosure</p>
  <h1>Independent, and not paid yet.</h1>
  <div class="prose stack">
    <p>
      Move-Out Desk compares college move-out and summer storage. The first campus is Texas A&M in
      College Station. This version is only storage.
    </p>
    <p>
      We are not Texas A&M, not the dorms, and not tied to Collegeboxes, Dorm Room Movers, U-Haul,
      CubeSmart, SpareBox, Anytime Storage, or Lock N Roll. Collegeboxes prints its own line: no
      active partnership with Texas A&M University, College Station. A company page is a source, not
      a recommendation.
    </p>
    <h2>What gets a number</h2>
    <p>
      A price, date, fee, or hour goes on the site only when we can open a public page that states
      it. The row keeps that link and the day we checked. If two pages disagree, we show both and
      mark the row sources disagree. If we cannot find the number, the cell says not yet verified.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not publish star ratings, review scores, or quotes from named students. Forum threads
      only tell us which questions people ask and which place names come up.
    </p>
    <h2>Paid links</h2>
    <p>
      None of the outbound links are paid. No affiliate program has been joined, and nothing here is
      written to earn a commission. Each company file has an <code>affiliateUrl</code> field, and
      today every one of those fields is empty.
    </p>
    <p>
      If a program is joined later, that field gets the tracking link. The site will point the
      button there, set <code>rel="sponsored nofollow"</code>, and show a Sponsored marker. An empty
      field stays a normal link to the company's own page. Pages will still say when a figure was
      checked, whether or not a link pays.
    </p>
    <h2>When a price goes stale</h2>
    <p>
      Storage prices move. A row that was right on November 18, 2026 can be wrong next week. There
      is no contact form on this version. The check that matters is the source link on the row. If
      you are about to pay, use the company's page, not our table, as the bill.
    </p>
    <h2>What this site does not do</h2>
    <ul class="clean">
      <li>No accounts, no booking, and no payment.</li>
      <li>No analytics, ad pixels, or other trackers.</li>
      <li>No made-up "most students choose" claims.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
